      "beat_id": "YTV01",
      "act": "VERDICT",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "am_onyx",
      "lead_silence_s": 0.5,
      "narration_text": "Let's recap with Claude. Three facts break classical theory: a sharp frequency threshold, instant emission, and electron energy set by frequency rather than intensity. Einstein's fix is that light arrives as photons, each carrying energy h times nu, and one photon strikes one electron. Kinetic energy equals h-nu minus the work function phi; below threshold that value is negative, so no electron escapes. Photons cannot pool their energy, so a blinding red lamp fails while a dim ultraviolet source ejects electrons immediately.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "hold",
